        "message": "Affected versions of org.apache.thrift:libthrift are vulnerable to Improper Certificate Validation / Improper Input Validation. An assert in the TSaslTransport class that verifies SASL handshake completion can be disabled when Java assertions are turned off, causing the isComplete check to be skipped. This allows a malicious or man-in-the-middle server to bypass SASL authentication and send unauthorized RPC calls.",
